  "configuration_id": "config_047",
  "reason": "Evidence: The top-3 configs all use scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l, with transformer aggregation slightly outperforming avgpool (0.725 vs 0.706) and weighted/concat fusion being nearly equivalent (0.725 vs 0.721). The image encoder has been held constant at imagenet_vit_l across all four experiments, leaving it as the largest untested dimension. Question: Does swapping imagenet_vit_l for resnet50 (config_047: scvi_n200, resnet50, transformer, weighted) improve or degrade performance relative to the current best (config_049, 0.725)? This isolates the image-encoder effect while keeping the proven-best RNA encoder, aggregation, and fusion. Why: With 5 experiments remaining, confirming or ruling out the image-encoder axis is the highest-value uncertainty to resolve. If resnet50 matches or beats imagenet_vit_l, it opens a new direction; if it lags significantly, it confirms imagenet_vit_l is near-optimal and we can focus remaining budget on profile-setting or fusion refinements."
}

